/*
 * pentagotchi_plugins.cpp
 *
 * MicroQuickJS host runtime + pentagotchi plugin bridge.
 *
 * The JS standard library used here is our own pentagotchi_stdlib (ROM tables
 * defined in lib/mquickjs/pentagotchi_stdlib_data.c, generated by
 * tools/mqjs-stdlib/). Every js_* symbol the tables reference is implemented
 * below with C linkage (see include/pentagotchi_plugins_api.h).
 *
 * Design notes:
 *  - The JS heap lives in PSRAM (fallback: internal RAM), 16-byte aligned.
 *  - Firmware events that can be raised from the WiFi RX ISR are queued in a
 *    little ring buffer and dispatched from poll() in the main loop.
 *  - Plugin instances are created with `new Plugin({...})` and tracked in a
 *    C array of JSGCRef (they must survive GC).
 */

